6}$.\nStep 6:  Solving for $[\\triangle CDE]$, we find $[\\triangle CDE] = \\frac{1}{16} \\times 6 = \\frac{6}{16} = \\frac{3}{8}$ square centimeters.\nStep 7:  Therefore, the area of $\\triangle CDE$ is $\\boxed{\\frac{3}{8}}$ square centimeters.\n\nThe final answer is: $\\boxed{\\frac{3}{8}}$", "decode_seconds": 4.418722451198846, "draft_calls": 123, "event": "benchmark_row", "input_tokens": 187, "method": "relay_p", "output_hash": "ef1608b17d9a38159f26aeacc8189177b796b22201576c6a82c1153d2d6c671e", "output_token_ids": [8468, 220, 16, 25, 220, 1226, 527, 2728, 430, 279, 3158, 315, 59060, 56214, 19921, 3, 374, 220, 21, 9518, 2960, 55336, 11, 323, 59060, 2017, 1074, 90, 1905, 11281, 23813, 2017, 1074, 90, 1170, 92, 13244, 1115, 3445, 430, 59060, 56214, 19921, 3, 323, 59060, 56214, 356, 1170, 3, 527, 4528, 43546, 627, 8468, 220, 17, 25, 220, 578, 2728, 11595, 400, 9740, 28, 19, 5002, 3, 24897, 430, 279, 11595, 315, 279, 12435, 11314, 315, 279, 1403, 43546, 374, 400, 19, 25, 16, 13244, 1115, 374, 264, 1401, 6710, 315, 2038, 430, 690, 1520, 603, 1505, 279, 3158, 315, 59060, 56214, 356, 1170, 3, 627, 8468, 220, 18, 25, 220, 8876, 279, 1403, 43546, 527, 4528, 11, 279, 11595, 315, 872, 5789, 374, 279, 9518, 315, 279, 11595, 315, 872, 12435, 11314, 13, 15636, 11, 279, 11595, 315, 279, 3158, 315, 59060, 56214, 356, 1170, 3, 311, 279, 3158, 315, 59060, 56214, 19921, 3, 374, 59060, 2414, 11781, 38118, 90, 16, 15523, 19, 11281, 1315, 30876, 17, 284, 1144, 38118, 90, 16, 15523, 845, 32816, 627, 8468, 220, 19, 25, 220, 2057, 1505, 279, 3158, 315, 59060, 56214, 356, 1170, 55976, 584, 649, 1005, 420, 11595, 323, 279, 2728, 3158, 315, 59060, 56214, 19921, 13244, 1226, 617, 59060, 38118, 90, 27148, 56214, 356, 1170, 14316, 90, 27148, 56214, 19921, 14316, 284, 1144, 38118, 90, 16, 15523, 845, 32816, 11, 1405, 400, 27148, 56214, 19921, 95380, 374, 279, 3158, 315, 59060, 56214, 19921, 3, 627, 8468, 220, 20, 25, 220, 3804, 3781, 10831, 279, 2728, 3158, 315, 59060, 56214, 19921, 3, 439, 2